3:T123f,<h2>Introduction</h2>
<p>Knee pain can significantly impact your daily life, limiting your mobility and affecting your overall quality of life. One lesser-known but crucial aspect of knee health is the cartilage, which serves as a cushion and allows for smooth joint movement. When cartilage is damaged, it can lead to pain and reduced mobility. Cartilage repair surgery in the knee is a specialized procedure aimed at restoring this vital tissue, alleviating pain, and improving function. In Hyderabad, top healthcare providers like <strong>Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy</strong> at <strong>Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad</strong> offer advanced options for cartilage repair.</p>

<h2>Understanding Cartilage Damage</h2>
<p>Knee cartilage can become damaged due to several reasons such as aging, sports injuries, or degenerative conditions like osteoarthritis. Articular cartilage, the type found in the knee, does not regenerate naturally, making surgical intervention critical for restoring knee function. Cartilage repair surgery becomes an important consideration when conservative treatments fail to relieve symptoms. Patients in <strong>Hyderabad</strong> seeking orthopedic care can find comprehensive solutions at facilities like <strong>Apollo Hospitals</strong>.</p>

<h2>Signs You Might Need Cartilage Repair Surgery</h2>
<ul>
<li>Persistent knee pain despite medication and therapy.</li>
<li>Swelling or discomfort in the knee joint.</li>
<li>Difficulty in performing regular activities such as walking or climbing stairs.</li>
<li>Knee locking or catching during movement.</li>
<li>A grinding sensation while moving the knee.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Treatment Options</h2>
<p>Cartilage repair surgery for the knee includes several advanced techniques, tailored to meet the specific needs of the patient. Some common procedures include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Microfracture Surgery:</strong> A minimally invasive technique that creates small holes in the bone to stimulate the growth of new cartilage.</li>
<li><strong>Autologous Chondrocyte Implantation (ACI):</strong> Involves harvesting cartilage cells, growing them in a lab, and re-implanting them into the damaged area.</li>
<li><strong>Osteochondral Autograft Transplantation (OATS):</strong> This procedure transfers healthy cartilage tissue from one part of the knee to repair the damaged area.</li>
<li><strong>Stem Cell Therapy:</strong> Utilizes regenerative cells to promote cartilage healing and regrowth.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each of these procedures has its own set of indications, benefits, and recovery timelines. Consulting with an experienced orthopedic surgeon like <strong>Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy</strong> can help determine the most suitable approach for your condition.</p>

<h2>Why Choose Dr. Harsha at Apollo Hospitals, Hyderabad?</h2>
<p>Choosing the right surgeon is crucial for the success of cartilage repair surgery. <strong>Dr. B Harsha Vardhana Reddy</strong> is a Senior Consultant Orthopedic Surgeon at <strong>Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Hyderabad</strong>, renowned for his extensive experience and expertise in cartilage repair and other orthopedic procedures. With access to state-of-the-art facilities and cutting-edge technology, patients can expect personalized care and optimal outcomes. Whether you are dealing with sports injuries, degenerative conditions, or unexplained knee pain, Dr. Harsha offers comprehensive treatment plans tailored to meet individual needs.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>Q: How long is the recovery period for cartilage repair surgery?</strong></p>
<p>A: The recovery period varies depending on the type of surgery performed. Typically, patients can expect to resume normal activities within 6 to 12 weeks, with full recovery taking several months.</p>

<p><strong>Q: Is cartilage repair surgery painful?</strong></p>
<p>A: Post-surgical pain is managed with medication and physical therapy. Most patients experience significant pain relief compared to their pre-surgery condition.</p>

<p><strong>Q: Are there any risks associated with cartilage repair surgery?</strong></p>
<p>A: As with any surgical procedure, there are risks such as infection, bleeding, or reactions to anesthesia. However, these are minimized by choosing an experienced surgeon and a reputable hospital.</p>

<h2>Book Your Appointment</h2>
<p>Don't let knee pain hold you back. Call <strong>Dr. Harsha at +91 99599 64567</strong> to schedule your appointment or visit <strong>Apollo Hospitals, Financial District, Nanakramguda, Hyderabad</strong>, for an expert consultation and take the first step towards pain-free mobility.</p>5:["slug","cartilage-repair-surgery-knee-hyderabad","d"]
